77 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E (In this assignment, a Multilayer Perceptron \(MLP\) neural network was implemented from scratch to solve a binary classification problem using the Wisconsin Diagnostic Breast Cancer dataset. The main objective of this work is to classify tumors as either benign or malignant based on thirty numerical features extracted from medical images.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
78 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 44 0 R
/E (The implementation includes manual forward propagation, backpropagation, and squared-loss error computation using Python and NumPy without relying on high-level machine learning or deep learning libraries. In addition, different learning rates and hidden layer sizes were evaluated to analyze their impact on the classification performance of the network.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
