144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (The model achieved an overall accuracy of 98.2% on the test set. Precision reached 100%, meaning that every case classified as malignant by the model was truly malignant, with no false positives. Recall was 95.2%, indicating that the model correctly identified 95.2% of all actual malignant cases while missing only a very small number of them.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (In medical classification tasks such as cancer detection, Recall is considered one of the most important evaluation metrics because missing a malignant case \(false negative\) can be far more dangerous than producing an unnecessary follow-up \(false positive\). The model performed very well in this regard, and the F1-Score of 97.6% reflects a strong balance between Precision and Recall.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
