200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (In this assignment, we built and trained an MLP from scratch using only NumPy, without relying on any machine learning frameworks, to classify breast cancer cases as benign or malignant. The network was trained using the squared-loss function and backpropagation with mini-batch gradient descent.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (The results showed that the model achieved a test accuracy of 98.2%, with a precision of 100%, recall of 95.2%, and an F1-Score of 97.6%. The lowest test loss was recorded at epoch 94. Among the learning rates tested, LR = 0.5 provided the best balance between convergence speed and training stability.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
202 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (Regarding hidden layer size, most tested values of k from 5 to 30 achieved an average test accuracy of approximately 99.1%, while k = 15 achieved a slightly lower accuracy of 98.95%. These results indicate that relatively small networks are sufficient for learning the patterns in this dataset effectively.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
203 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 50 0 R
/E (Overall, the MLP implemented in this assignment demonstrated strong generalization performance, no significant overfitting, and promising performance for breast cancer diagnosis support.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
